      "nets": ["Net-(U8-Pad2)", "Net-(U8-Pad4)", "/V_EC"],
      "observed": "U8 (74LVC1G34) is inserted between U4 pin 19 (SCL_1) and M3 pin 2 (TX/SCL). U8 pin 2 is connected to U4.19, U8 pin 4 is connected to M3.2 and R19.1. U8 is powered from +3V3 (pin 5).",
      "expected": "Spec says U4 (EC isolator) connects directly to M3 (EZO-EC) on the isolated I2C bus. No buffer should be present. The isolated SCL line should be a direct bidirectional connection with a pull-up to /V_EC.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"118\") (name \"Net-(U8-Pad2)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"19\") (pinfunction \"SCL_{1}\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) (node (ref \"U8\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"input\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"119\") (name \"Net-(U8-Pad4)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"M3\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"TX/SCL\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) (node (ref \"R19\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"U8\") (pin \"4\") (pintype \"output\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "U3 (pH) and U4 (EC) each present a secondary isolated I2C pair (/SDA_pH//SCL_pH, /SDA_EC//SCL_EC) that connects directly to M2 (EZO-pH) and M3 (EZO-EC) respectively"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Breaks I2C bidirectionality and level compatibility; U8 input lacks pull-up, output drives against 5V pull-up, likely preventing EC sensor communication.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["U5", "U6", "U7"],
      "pins": ["U5.20", "U6.20", "U7.20"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(U5-STDBY-Pad20)", "unconnected-(U6-STDBY-Pad20)", "unconnected-(U7-STDBY-Pad20)"],
      "observed": "STDBY pins of all three TMC2209 drivers are left unconnected.",
      "expected": "TMC2209 STDBY pin has internal pull-up and must be pulled low for normal operation. It should be tied to GND.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"144\") (name \"unconnected-(U5-STDBY-Pad20)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"20\") (pinfunction \"STDBY\") (pintype \"input+no_connect\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"150\") (name \"unconnected-(U6-STDBY-Pad20)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"20\") (pinfunction \"STDBY\") (pintype \"input+no_connect\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"155\") (name \"unconnected-(U7-STDBY-Pad20)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"U7\") (pin \"20\") (pinfunction \"STDBY\") (pintype \"input+no_connect\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "All three stepper drivers remain in standby mode, disabling motor outputs; dosing pumps will not run.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["U5", "U6", "U7"],
      "pins": ["U5.9", "U5.10", "U6.9", "U6.10", "U7.9", "U7.10"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(U5-MS1{slash}AD0-Pad9)", "unconnected-(U5-MS2{slash}AD1-Pad10)", "unconnected-(U6-MS1{slash}AD0-Pad9)", "+3V3"],
      "observed": "U5 MS1/AD0 and MS2/AD1 are unconnected. U6 MS1/AD0 is unconnected, MS2/AD1 is tied to +3V3. U7 MS1/AD0 and MS2/AD1 are tied to +3V3.",
      "expected": "For a shared UART bus, each TMC2209 must have a unique address set by MS1/AD0 and MS2/AD1, typically tied to GND or VCC_IO. Floating pins are invalid.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"141\") (name \"unconnected-(U5-MS1{slash}AD0-Pad9)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"9\") (pinfunction \"MS1/AD0\") (pintype \"input+no_connect\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"142\") (name \"unconnected-(U5-MS2{slash}AD1-Pad10)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"10\") (pinfunction \"MS2/AD1\") (pintype \"input+no_connect\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"148\") (name \"unconnected-(U6-MS1{slash}AD0-Pad9)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"9\") (pinfunction \"MS1/AD0\") (pintype \"input+no_connect\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"10\") (pinfunction \"MS2/AD1\") (pintype \"input\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U7\") (pin \"9\") (pinfunction \"MS1/AD0\") (pintype \"input\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "UART addresses are undefined or conflicting, preventing proper UART communication with the drivers.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain multiple anomalies: an extra buffer (U8) inserted in the isolated EC I2C SCL line, and all three TMC2209 stepper drivers have their STDBY pins floating (forcing standby) and their MS1/MS2 address pins incorrectly configured for a shared UART bus."
}

